{
 "final_text": "**The adaptation did not produce a promotable policy. The promotion gate rejected the checkpoint `scratch~a7ee2c-s7`.**\n\n**Measured failure of the deployed policy (P-static-b, val-target-v1, 60 episodes)**\n- Success rate was 0.367 and collision rate was 0.483.\n- Of the collisions, 21 were with the mover and 8 with static obstacles. There were no wall collisions.\n- 9 episodes timed out.\n- The authored hypotheses are not measured causes. They say mover collisions *may* mean weak yielding and static collisions *may* mean weak static avoidance.\n\n**Parent selection (rule ew-select-3, decision `deci-20261015060348-a7ee2c`)**\n- The rule chose `train_from_scratch`. No existing checkpoint was selected as a parent.\n- Scratch had p_reach 0.2308 (2 of 11 applicable scratch trials reached threshold).\n- The checkpoints P-static-a, P-cross-a and P-open-a each had p_reach 0.1429 (0 of 5 trials reached threshold).\n- P-static-b had p_reach 0.0714 (0 of 12 trials).\n- P-mirror was rejected because its contract does not match (the ray order differs).\n- The decision listed no candidates needing evaluation, so I queued no extra matched validations.\n\n**Training (seed 7, 150k PPO steps, run once, no retry)**\n- The job produced the child `scratch~a7ee2c-s7`. It used 151,552 steps in total.\n- It did **not** reach the target threshold (`threshold_reached` was false).\n- Its final val-target-v1 result was a success rate of 0.867 and a collision rate of 0.133. Of those collisions, 2 were static and 6 were mover.\n\n**Retained-behaviour validation (40 episodes each)**\n\n| Suite | Success rate | Collision rate | Gate requirement | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| val-open-v1 | 0.725 | 0.0 | success \u2265 0.9 | Fail. The other episodes timed out (27.5%). |\n| val-static-v1 | 0.95 | 0.025 | success \u2265 0.75, collisions \u2264 0.1 | Pass |\n| val-crossing-v1 | 0.725 | 0.175 | success \u2265 0.75, collisions \u2264 0.15 | Fail. All 7 collisions were with the mover. |\n\n**Promotion (`prom-20261015060506-9a3c7a`)**\n- Verdict: rejected. Three of the four suites failed.\n- val-target-v1 passed on success (0.87 against a minimum of 0.8) but failed on collisions (0.13 against a maximum of 0.1).\n- val-open-v1 and val-crossing-v1 failed as shown in the table above.\n\n**Evidence export**\n- Bundle: `scratch~a7ee2c-s7-556ec083bc85.zip`\n- sha256: `083a32973e5b1a9853ad62dae15a3eee5e60e913368ae531a13a60d935a50eda`\n- Artifact hash: `556ec083bc8589363d034745bac670bf7e0afb17fedf138ea0fd8b8797066baa`\n\nThe new checkpoint is much better than the deployed policy on the target suite (success 0.87 against 0.37). It still fails the gate, and P-static-b remains deployed. The mover collisions still appear in the target and crossing results. That fits the yielding hypothesis, but this run did not test that hypothesis.",
